        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $b$ be the number of blue chairs. There are $b+3$ red chairs and $2b+3$ chairs altogether.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{b}{2b+3}&=\\frac{7}{15}\\\\15b&=7(2b+3)\\\\15b&=14b+21\\\\b&=21\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere are $21$ blue chairs.",
